Format: Layer, Start, End, Style, Name, MarginL, MarginR, MarginV, Effect, Text
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:05.16,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Let's begin with a quick\Npreview of programming with\Nlive probes in Hazel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.16,0:00:14.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}The tutorial will then cover Hazel\Nand each probe feature in detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.20,0:00:16.13,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}First, manual probes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.13,0:00:18.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Right-click any expression\Nor pattern...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.40,0:00:22.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}...and choose Add probe\N(or press Cmd/Ctrl+E).
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.18,0:00:24.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Its value appears at the end\Nof the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.90,0:00:29.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Not just variables: here,\Nan arithmetic expression...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.21,0:00:32.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}...and here, a whole case\Nexpression.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.20,0:00:35.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}By default, a probe shows\None value at a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.61,0:00:38.43,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}With a sample selected, press\NSpace for Many mode...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.43,0:00:42.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}...which shows every value\Nfrom the run.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.60,0:00:44.75,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Click a sample to make it\Nthe focus...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.75,0:00:55.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}...and the other probes highlight\Ntheir samples from that same call.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.40,0:00:58.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,272)}Rather than placing every\Nprobe by hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.08,0:01:02.18,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}...press Cmd/Ctrl+P to turn\Non Auto Probe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.18,0:01:08.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}It puts one probe on each line\Nthat has something to probe.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.00,0:01:14.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}Unlike some other environments,\NHazel runs incomplete programs.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.00,0:01:17.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}This hole is the unfinished\Nbody of watering_amount.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.50,0:01:22.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}Each call returns that hole,\Nwhich the tests show too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.00,0:01:23.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}Start typing...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.10,0:01:32.29,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\pos(938,530)}...and the feedback stays live,\Neven while the code is incomplete.
